Portions of scripts/native_usage.py are adapted from CodexBar v0.67.0
(https://github.com/steipete/CodexBar, e0286a895055e60ddaefa6a5f176f246aa2f05e4):
- CodexOAuthUsageFetcher.swift and CodexOAuthCredentials.swift: Codex auth-file
  fields, read-only WHAM usage request, general and additional window fields.
- AntigravityStatusProbe.swift and AntigravityQuotaSummaryParser.swift: existing
  local quota-summary RPC and quota-bucket decoding. No launch or OAuth flow.
The optional Antigravity OAuth summary reader interoperates with the provider's
existing sign-in and Google quota-summary endpoint, observed in T3 Code's
Antigravity usage integration; no T3 Code source is redistributed.
- tests/fixtures/native-usage/agy-local-quota.json uses the upstream test
  response shapes, with synthetic values and a separate Argon bucket.

The macOS menu bar app in menubar/mac/ is adapted from CodexBar v0.67.0 (same commit),
under the MIT notice below:
- UsageProgressBar.swift: the Canvas progress bar with its punched-out pace stripe.
- MenuCardView.swift, UsageMenuCardHeaderAndUsageSectionView.swift and
  MenuCardMetricRow.swift: card header, labelled usage rows with "% used" and reset
  line; UsagePaceText.swift: the pace line; MenuCardView layout metrics.
- ProviderSwitcherButtons.swift and StatusItemController+SwitcherViews.swift:
  provider tiles (icon over title, filled when selected, mini usage bar under each),
  and StatusItemController+Menu.swift: the 310 pt card width and hosted-card menu.
- IconRenderer.swift: the idea of a two-bar usage icon in the menu bar.
Each ported Swift file keeps CodexBar's copyright in its header. The menu text and colours
are Crossfeed's; the CodexBar name and logo are not used. The bundled fonts in
menubar/mac/Resources/Fonts (Commissioner, Martian Mono) are under the SIL Open Font
License 1.1; the licence files sit next to them.

